# P6 · Wearable capture and advanced AI · Weeks 33–42 (after hardware is stable) · R6 Clip
# exit: 1 device, consent, offline, overlap test suites pass · 2 battery lasts a full clinic day · 3 revoke < 1 minute
# nfr:  1 visible recording light; start/stop bound to an encounter · 2 signed firmware + secure update path
# pkg:  1 device kit + quick-start · 2 fleet guide for admins
# dep:  1 hardware partner + certification · 2 language model quality per language

@epic MDV-P6-E01 | Medvya clip lifecycle | P6-01 | Pair, check, buffer, update and revoke the clip safely.
@epic MDV-P6-E02 | Advanced AI | P6-02, P6-03, P6-05 | Earpiece-only assistant, mixed-language notes and stronger AI QA.
@epic MDV-P6-E03 | Outbound voice and R6 gate | P6-04 | Reminder/recall calls and waitlist fill; R6 release.

=== MDV-P6-001
title: Hardware partner, device certification and regulated-device classification advice
type: Chore
epic: MDV-P6-E01
prd: P6-01
covers: dep:1
priority: MUST
roles: Founder
labels: hardware, regulatory
estimate: 2
weeks: 33-34
confidence: 45 | Hardware partner not chosen (decision default: defer until phone metrics are met); CDSCO/UAE classification advice pending.
sources: PRD v2 P6 dependency 1, open decision "Wearable hardware partner"; design/uploads/DoctorMate_Software_Architecture_Azure_India_UAE_2026 (1).md §10 (regulated-device check, ESP32-S3 limits)
desc:
Select the hardware partner (ESP32-S3 prototype limits: BLE control path, Wi-Fi or phone audio), obtain radio/safety certifications needed per country and classification advice (India CDSCO, UAE) for the intended use (recording accessory, human-approved documentation).
ac:
- Partner contract and BOM recorded; certification plan with dates.
- Written classification advice for the final intended use and marketing claims.
- Go/no-go decision recorded against the phone-capture metrics from P3.

=== MDV-P6-002
title: Clip pairing with code match and microphone self-test (W-01)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P6-E01
prd: P6-01
screens: W-01
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: clip, pairing, ble
estimate: 4
weeks: 34-36
depends: MDV-P6-001
confidence: 60 | Flow designed; depends on firmware/BLE capabilities.
sources: design/Medvya Mobile and Tablet (Wearable pairing); design/Medvya Wireframes (W-01)
desc:
Hold button 3 s → LED pulses → companion shows 4-digit code that must match the clip's LED pattern → mic self-test ("say testing") → pair to the doctor (DEVICE_PAIRING valid 90 days). Clip becomes selectable at consent (A-02).
ac:
- Pairing requires explicit code confirmation; mismatches abort and are logged.
- Pairing expires after 90 days and requires re-pairing.
- Self-test failure blocks pairing with guidance.
- Paired clip appears in A-02 device list with battery and firmware.

=== MDV-P6-003
title: Clip capture bound to encounter and consent with visible recording light (capture FSM)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P6-E01
prd: P6-01
screens: W-01
covers: nfr:1, exit:1
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: clip, capture, consent
estimate: 4
weeks: 36-37
depends: MDV-P6-002, MDV-P3-006
confidence: 60 | Firmware-enforced LED and nonce-bound sessions depend on hardware.
sources: docs/03-architecture/state-machines.md#capture-fsm-p3-p6; PRD v2 P6 NFR 1
desc:
Start/stop only for the verified current encounter with consent; device-bound session start with nonce; LED on throughout capture (firmware-enforced); chunks uploaded via phone relay or Wi-Fi with integrity hashes; never attachable to two encounters.
ac:
- The clip cannot record without an active encounter + consent authorisation (server and firmware).
- LED is on whenever the microphone captures (hardware test).
- Replayed or out-of-sequence chunks are rejected.
- Device, consent and overlap test suites pass (exit gate 1).

=== MDV-P6-004
title: Device health, battery, encrypted offline buffer, upload conflicts and staged firmware updates (W-02)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P6-E01
prd: P6-01
screens: W-02
covers: nfr:2, exit:1, exit:2
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Practice admin
labels: clip, firmware, offline
estimate: 4
weeks: 37-39
depends: MDV-P6-003
confidence: 58 | Signed OTA and battery life depend on hardware maturity.
sources: design/Medvya Wireframes (W-02); design/Medvya Clinician App (W-02 Devices)
desc:
Device page: battery %, BLE status, firmware version, encrypted offline queue ("2 recordings in encrypted queue"), Sync now, staged firmware update (1.4.2 → 1.5.0) with signed images and rollback/anti-rollback; upload conflict (same session on phone + clip) keeps both and the clinician picks.
ac:
- Firmware updates only accept signed images; tampered images are rejected (test).
- Offline recordings stay encrypted on the device and sync later without loss (offline suite; exit gate 1).
- Battery lasts a full clinic day (≥ 8 h mixed use) in a field test (exit gate 2).
- Upload conflicts surface a choice and never silently merge.

=== MDV-P6-005
title: Loss/theft revoke effective in under one minute (W-03)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P6-E01
prd: P6-01
screens: W-03
covers: exit:3
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Practice admin
labels: clip, security
estimate: 2
weeks: 39
depends: MDV-P6-004
confidence: 72 | Server-side revocation is in our control; device key wipe depends on firmware.
sources: design/Medvya Wireframes (W-03)
desc:
Revoke with reason (lost/stolen/retired): binding revoked, keys/tokens invalidated, queued audio on the device becomes unreadable, audit event and admin notification.
ac:
- After revoke, the device cannot authenticate or upload within 60 seconds (exit gate 3 test).
- Revocation is audited and the admin notified.
- A revoked device must be re-provisioned to be used again.

=== MDV-P6-006
title: Private voice assistant through earpiece only (A-07)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P6-E02
prd: P6-02
screens: A-07
priority: SHOULD
roles: Doctor
labels: ai, voice, privacy
estimate: 4
weeks: 38-40
depends: MDV-P6-003
confidence: 55 | Requires private audio route detection and low-latency speech; safety constraints strict.
sources: design/Medvya Clinical Screens (A-07); design/Medvya Wireframes (A-07)
desc:
Doctor taps or hotword to ask (e.g. "last eGFR"); answers shown as text first and spoken only through a connected private earpiece ("whisper mode"); if the earpiece disconnects, the assistant turns off; answers come only from the patient's verified chart with source.
ac:
- The assistant never speaks through the room speaker; disconnecting the earpiece disables it immediately (test).
- Every answer cites its chart source; no diagnosis or treatment advice.
- Queries and answers are audited without storing audio beyond policy.

=== MDV-P6-007
title: Multilingual notes: Arabic, English, Hindi and Malayalam incl. mixed-language consultations
type: Story
epic: MDV-P6-E02
prd: P6-03
screens: A-04
covers: dep:2
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: ai, languages
estimate: 4
weeks: 35-38
depends: MDV-P3-018
confidence: 55 | Model quality per language is a stated dependency.
sources: PRD v2 P6-03, dependency 2
desc:
Extend transcription and drafting to Arabic and Malayalam (and mixed AR/EN, ML/EN, HI/EN) with original and translation side by side in transcript and evidence; per-language evaluation sets.
ac:
- Per-language evaluation sets meet the same safety gate (0 fabricated medicines/doses).
- Transcript and evidence show original-language text beside the translation for each language.
- Language quality results are documented per language before enabling it per tenant.

=== MDV-P6-008
title: Stronger AI QA: per-language evaluation sets, clinician trust metrics, red-team prompts on uploaded documents
type: Task
epic: MDV-P6-E02
prd: P6-05
covers: exit:1
priority: MUST
roles: Developer, Clinical advisor
labels: ai-quality, red-team
estimate: 3
weeks: 36-40
depends: MDV-P6-007, MDV-P5-014
confidence: 70 | Extends the P3 harness.
sources: PRD v2 P6-05
desc:
Per-language evaluation sets, ongoing clinician trust metrics, red-team prompt-injection tests against uploaded documents and transcripts, overlap/speaker suites for multi-speaker clip recordings.
ac:
- CI runs per-language and red-team suites on every prompt/model change.
- Overlap and speaker-attribution suites pass for clip recordings (exit gate 1).
- Trust metrics are reported monthly per clinician cohort.

=== MDV-P6-009
title: Outbound voice reminder and recall calls; waitlist fill from cancellations
type: Story
epic: MDV-P6-E03
prd: P6-04
screens: N-10
priority: SHOULD
roles: Patient, Receptionist
labels: voice, outbound
estimate: 3
weeks: 39-41
depends: MDV-P5-015
confidence: 58 | Builds on the P5 voice assistant; consent for automated calls per country must be confirmed.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (G-06 outbound calls); PRD v2 P6-04
desc:
Automated reminder/recall calls for patients without WhatsApp, and calls/messages to waitlisted patients when a slot frees; same identity and safety rules as inbound.
ac:
- Calls are placed only to patients with a consent/opt-in for calls.
- Waitlist fill offers slots in order and books only on explicit confirmation.
- Call outcomes are logged as contact attempts and never close care tasks by themselves.

